course: dictionary
lesson: 7920
title: Re, the little word with three jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word re has three jobs. It can be a short word at the top of a letter or email, the start of a longer word, or a musical note. Look at the words around it to find out which job it is doing.
explain: At the top of an email, «Re: school trip» means about the school trip, so it is a reply on that subject. Here re is a preposition, a small word that shows what something is about.
explain: When re is at the front of a longer word, it is a prefix. Re- means again or back, so redo means do again and return means go back. Split the word, check the first part, then read the rest: rewrite means write again.
explain: Re can also be a note in music. In do, re, mi, it is the second note of the scale. Context tells you which job it has: a letter, a longer word, or a song.
fact: Re can be a short word meaning about or on the subject of, used at the top of letters and emails.
fact: «Re: school trip» means about the school trip.
fact: The prefix re- means again or back, as in redo, rewrite, replay and return.
fact: Re is the second note of the musical scale do, re, mi, and it is also spelt ray.
fact: Re is often a fragment of a longer word, so check the whole word before you decide what it means.
exercise: «Re: homework» is at the top of an email. What does re mean here? | Before | Again | *About | A musical note
exercise: What does re- mean in «replay»? | Not playing | *Play again | Play before | A musical note
exercise: In the song do, re, mi, what is re? | *The second note of the scale | The third note of the scale | The first note of the scale | A kind of drum
test: In «Re: your birthday plans», what does re mean? | Back home | The first note of a song | Again | *About the subject
test: What does «rewrite» mean? | Write wrongly | Write before | Write under | *Write again
exam: Which word uses re- to mean again? | preview | *replay | bicycle | dislike
